Fresh exact-head measurement for `d391a663a`:

- live A/B: **36/36 independently verified outcomes**, 0 hard-invariant violations;
- baseline used 2 provider decisions; guarded used **1 provider + 1 guarded-completion** in both Python and TypeScript;
- guarded step 2 had `provider_decision_ms = 0` in every cell;
- paired verified-outcome delta: median **-182.72 ms** across 18 pairs, bootstrap 95% CI **[-210.72, -83.97]**;
- step-2 provider-decision delta: median **-176.25 ms**, 18/18 guarded cells faster.

This is still the narrow claim from the PR: remove one provider decision on the two-step fixture while preserving fresh observation/ref authority. No broader speedup claim.
